A('1965-0117-hoaiduc', '1965-01-17', VH, 'Bình Thuận. Region 6\'s Battalion 186 ambushes and destroys a Civil Guard company and three Self-Defense platoons marching from Hoài Đức to Mê Pu, Jan. 17, and then takes the Bắc Núi hamlet, the last next to the subsector, and besieges the Hoài Đức district seat.', 'III, 401–02', place='me-pu', also=OP)
A('1965-0120-baulach', '1965-01-20', VH, 'Gia Định. Companies 707 and 200 of the Saigon–Gia Định Region fight together, Jan. 20, and stop two Saigon main-force battalions sweeping the Bàu Lách hamlet, Nhuận Đức commune, in the Củ Chi tunnels area: 166 out of action.', 'III, 395–96', place='bau-lach', also=OP)
A('1965-0206-vietan', '1965-02-06', VH, 'Quảng Nam. The night of Feb. 6–7 Region 5\'s Regiment 1 attacks the Việt An strongpoint, a key post on a hill at the junction of Routes 105 and 16, 8 km south of the Quế Sơn district seat.', 'III, 400', to='1965-02-07', place='viet-an', band_='night', also=OP)
A('1965-0207-pleiku', '1965-02-07', VH, 'Gia Lai. The night of Feb. 7 the Region\'s Sapper Battalion 407 and Battalion 334 of Regiment 320 take a string of Civil Guard posts west of Pleiku and the Plây Mơrông commando border post: 100 killed. In the same weeks Regiment 101 takes Đắk Giao, shells the Đắk Pét base and breaks Route 14 north of Kon Tum.', 'III, 399–400', place='pleiku', band_='night', also=OP)
A('1965-0210-lo-o', '1965-02', VH, 'Bình Thuận. Early in February Region 6\'s main forces destroy the Lồ Ô strongpoint at Tánh Linh and badly hurt the subsector; 1,000 people of the Đồng Me concentration area rise and go back to the base.', 'III, 402', when='Feb., early', place='lo-o', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1965-0223-hoaiduc2', '1965-02-23', VH, 'Bình Thuận. The night of Feb. 23 part of the Region\'s main force with Hàm Tân\'s local troops attacks the Hiệp Hòa hamlet and badly hurts two companies come from the subsector; Feb. 23 the garrison of the Hoài Đức subsector leaves its post and runs to Võ Đắc. All Hoài Đức district and most of Tánh Linh, over 35,000 people, are free.', 'III, 402', place='hoai-duc', band_='night', also=OP, check='the history gives both acts on Feb. 23, the attack on the hamlet by night and the subsector\'s abandoning.')
A('1965-0330-op129', '1965-03-30', VH, 'Kon Tum. Mar. 30 Regiment 101 finishes the fight against Saigon\'s operation 129, begun to retake the posts lost in northern Kon Tum (Regiments 40 and 42, Ranger Battalion 21): it destroys most of Battalion 21 and a company of the 1st Battalion, 42d Regiment and shoots down three aircraft; the Saigon forces withdraw and the garrisons of Đắk Tả, Đắk Vân, Mỏ Lẹt and Măng Bút run.', 'III, 400', place='kontum', also=OP, check='the operation\'s start not given.')
V('cal.1965-03-30.vietnam', 'A', 'the charge 150 kg of high explosive in a car driven into the main gate of the five-story embassy, set off by hand; 132 Americans and others killed or wounded, Deputy Ambassador U. Alexis Johnson badly wounded, Taylor away; the history cites the Pentagon Papers for its being the most direct Communist act against the Americans', 'III, 396–97')
